# Disclosure term list — FORMAT EXAMPLE
#
# Copy to `.disclosure-terms.local` and replace these placeholders with the real
# names. The .local file is gitignored and MUST stay that way: a tracked file
# listing real companies is a public index of every process you are in, which is
# strictly worse than the leak it is meant to prevent.
#
# Format:
#   - one term per line
#   - blank lines ignored
#   - `#` starts a comment, inline or full-line
#   - terms are word-bounded and case-insensitive, so "Acme" matches "Acme" and
#     "ACME" but never "Acmestone"
#   - multi-word terms are fine: "North Ridge Partners"
#
# Checked by scripts/check-disclosure.mjs, which runs in `npm run check` and
# therefore blocks the deploy. When the .local file is absent the gate still
# runs, checking only the committed generic patterns, so CI never depends on an
# untracked file.
#
# Every name below is fictional and exists only to show the shape.

# Companies in an active process
Acme Dynamics
Northwind Systems
Contoso

# Agencies and intermediaries
North Ridge Partners
Blue Harbor Talent

# Prior employers and their internal products
Initech
Umbrella Analytics
Project Nightingale          # an internal tool name, not a company
